- op: discuss  # 4cee
  at: '2026-04-17T09:24:53Z'  # 4cee
  by: agent  # 4cee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4cee
  clock: 4  # 4cee
  nonce: 4cee  # 4cee
  message: "Investigation 2026-04-17: scoping the refactor size before starting.\n\nThe path-to-ID construction is distributed across all language analyzers, not centralized. Each analyzer (py.py, go.py, rust.py, java.py, etc.) has its own '_make_symbol_id' helper that inlines 'str(file_path)' directly into an f-string. Examples:\n- packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py:1840 → id=_make_symbol_id(str(py_file), 1, end_line, ...)\n- Similar pattern in analyze/base.py:293 for 'make_node_id' (but that helper has 0 callers — dead code signal for follow-up).\n- Linkers construct their own IDs too: view_template.py:246, crypto_flow.py:279-280, message_dispatch.py:254-255, js_module.py:216, openapi.py:315.\n\nImplications for WI-hopug:\n1. ~35 analyzer files plus 6+ linker files need to accept a repo_root argument and relativize paths before formatting IDs.\n2. Every test fixture that hard-codes a path-in-id string will need updating.\n3. Alternative: post-process at the JSON emit boundary (cli.py's run_behavior_map). Single site, but must rewrite node IDs AND every edge src/dst string reference consistently. Brittle — any subcommand reading the behavior map (slice, explain, routes, io-boundaries, etc.) must all observe the rewrite.\n4. ID stability across runs from different machines is the real goal. Post-processing preserves that per-output-file; refactor preserves it everywhere internally.\n\nRecommendation: refactor at the analyzer layer, not post-process. Introduce a RepoRoot argument threaded through analyzer.analyze(repo_root=...) and have '_make_symbol_id' in each analyzer compute 'str(path.relative_to(repo_root))'. Covers all downstream consumers without per-subcommand rewrite code.\n\nEstimate: 4-8 hours including test-fixture updates. Deferring to a dedicated session rather than jamming into an end-of-session slot."  # 4cee
